<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-18242] allow 'lfs df -m/-o' to specify one MDT/OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18242</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;As an extension to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17516" title="add &amp;#39;lfs df --mdt&amp;#39; and &amp;#39;lfs df --ost&amp;#39; options" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17516"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17516&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; it would be useful if "&lt;tt&gt;lfs df &amp;#45;&amp;#45;mdt/&amp;#45;&amp;#45;ost&lt;/tt&gt;" took an optional argument "&lt;tt&gt;&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;INDEX&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/tt&gt;" to specify a single MDT/OST index for which to print the usage.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That would avoid a lot of cases where "&lt;tt&gt;lfs df | grep ...&lt;/tt&gt;" is used in test scripts to find space usage for a particular target, and is likely equally useful for end users.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
